Project: Anomaly-based cyberattack detection for smart electricity meters.
Scope: consumption-based attacks only. Python, pandas, scikit-learn, Streamlit.
Data: London Smart Meters subset (50-200 meters, hourly) with synthetic injected attacks
(scaling, zeroing, spikes, ramp-down). Labels and attack start times are recorded.
Models: Isolation Forest (train on normal data only), Random Forest (class_weight='balanced'),
z-score baseline.
Rules: split train/test by TIME, never randomly. Keep code in src/ modules with docstrings.
Metrics: accuracy, precision, recall, F1, false-alarm rate = FP/(FP+TN),
detection latency = first flagged reading minus attack start.
Keep it simple. No extra frameworks. Set random seeds for reproducibility.